Assume $\phi$ is drawn from $D_{\Phi}(n,k)$. Let $\alpha = \frac{\lfloor n\lg(k)/(16k) \rfloor}{n}$.

Conditioned on there being at least one satisfying assignment to $\phi$, \HammDist($\phi$) will return some satisfying assignment with probability at least $ 1-3\cdot 2^{-n/(3\ln(2)2^k)}$.

Conditioned on there being no satisfying assignment to $\phi$, \HammDist($\phi$) will return False with probability $1$. 

\HammDist($\phi$) will run 
in time 
